Give a monitor that returns mid-lock its own lockdead_screen_delay

misc:lockdead_screen_delay is measured once, from when the session was
locked. A monitor that comes back later in the lock -- a display waking from
DPMS off whose link dropped, a dock re-enumerating after resume -- has no lock
surface on its first frames, and since the lock is already older than the
delay, Hyprland draws lockdead on it at once. The lock client is alive and is
about to cover the new output, so every wake flashes "lockscreen app died".

Track, per monitor, when it was first drawn without a mapped lock surface, and
draw lockdead only once both the lock and that monitor are past the delay. The
grace starts afresh when the monitor is connected, disconnected or changes
DPMS, since monitor ids are reused and a waking display is a returning one. A
timer redraws the monitor when its grace runs out, so a client that is alive
but never covers it still gets lockdead. A client that dies drops the session
lock and shows lockdead at once as before, and a denied lock is unchanged.
Workspaces stay hidden behind the primer during the grace exactly as before.

Not yet upstream.

